WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.589
We’ve been using Apple’s new 2019 MacBook
Air for about a week, and we can say that

00:00:04.589 --> 00:00:09.480
it basically feels the same as the last years’
model, but unlike last year, quite a few things

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:12.230
have changed that will greatly impact your
buying decision.

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:16.600
If you’ve seen our recent Which MacBook
should you buy in 2019 video, you probably

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:21.170
already know that the new base 13” MacBook
Pro is the king of value when it comes to

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:26.270
performance, being much faster than the MacBook
Air and offering basically twice as much performance

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:27.270
per dollar.

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:31.590
So in the case that you really want the most
performance you can get, you should obviously

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.170
buy the MacBook Pro instead.

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:37.149
But what if you don’t really care that much
about performance, what if you value other

00:00:37.149 --> 00:00:42.399
things, like battery life and typing experience
and saving a couple hundred dollars?

00:00:42.399 --> 00:00:46.789
That’s the case for a lot of people out
there, for people who just need a basic, reliable

00:00:46.789 --> 00:00:51.149
and premium laptop, to students, writers or
programmers.

00:00:51.149 --> 00:00:55.379
And yes, we did just release a brand new video
talking about how it actually makes sense

00:00:55.379 --> 00:01:01.089
for some people to buy an iPad Pro over a
MacBook Air, but if you’re digging the traditional

00:01:01.089 --> 00:01:06.750
laptop feel and you need macOS, the Air still
makes a lot of sense to buy, despite being

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:11.090
the only MacBook in Apple’s 2019 lineup
with a dual-core processor.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:15.520
And in the real world, unless you’re doing
power-demanding productivity tasks, the MacBook

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:18.020
Air is still fast enough for a lot of people.

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:22.520
For example, people have been using dual-core
MacBook Airs for programming in apps like

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:26.390
Xcode for years, despite being much slower
than the MacBook Pros.

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:30.729
Sure, it won’t get the job done as quickly,
but it still gets it done.

00:01:30.729 --> 00:01:35.840
And for productivity work like this, the MacBook
Pros brighter and more color accurate display

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:37.590
doesn’t really matter.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:42.000
On the plus side, the MacBook Air does get
True Tone technology this year, a feature

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.499
which automatically adjusts the white balance
of the display to match the environment you’re

00:01:46.499 --> 00:01:50.609
in, so if you’re in a very warm-lit dark
room, the screen won’t blast you with a

00:01:50.609 --> 00:01:52.539
bunch of distracting blue light.

00:01:52.539 --> 00:01:56.590
This is a really great feature, especially
for people who spend a lot of time typing

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:57.799
on their MacBook.

00:01:57.799 --> 00:02:00.789
And for typing, the MacBook Air is the best
you can get this year.

00:02:00.789 --> 00:02:05.119
That’s mainly due to the fact that the keyboard
actually sloped downward towards the front

00:02:05.119 --> 00:02:10.140
edge, which makes typing a lot more comfortable
to the flat straight-edged MacBook Pro.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:15.000
Now here’s where the drama comes in, Apple’s
butterfly keyboard is still equipped on this

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:20.430
MacBook, which is known for having dead or
stuck key issues, and it’s a MAJOR reason

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:22.730
why people think twice about buying it.

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:35.140
But is this a major deal?

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:55.610
We actually don’t think so, for a few reasons.

00:02:55.610 --> 00:03:00.810
We’ve been using and testing Apple’s butterfly
keyboard-equipped MacBooks ever since the

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:06.750
original 2015 Retina MacBook, and so far,
out of around 30 MacBooks we’ve tested,

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:11.430
with 5 of them being long-term, we’ve only
had issues with one MacBook, the original

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:13.570
2015 12” Retina.

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:17.440
Other than that, we’ve experienced none
of the issues at all, and the best part about

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:23.440
the 2019 MacBook Air is that it features Apple’s
4th-generation butterfly keys, with new materials

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:25.530
that are supposed to be more reliable.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:29.740
This version of keys has been on the market
for around 2 months, and so far, we haven’t

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:34.070
heard of a single report of keyboard issues
on the 2019 MacBooks.

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:39.330
So we’re now pretty confident that if you
buy a 2019 MacBook Air, you probably won’t

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:40.450
experience any issues.

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:45.570
And just to give you peace of mind, Apple
is giving you a free 4 year keyboard-replacement

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:51.100
warranty on any new MacBook, and to be completely
honest, if your keyboard is affected, it’ll

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:55.260
probably happen within the first 4 years,
so I wouldn’t worry about it.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.680
Now here’s something great about the MacBook
Air.

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:02.440
It’s now the only new MacBook that comes
with function keys, so if you absolutely hate

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:06.730
the Touch Bar that now comes on every MacBook
Pro, you can go with the Air instead.

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:12.450
And as a bonus, you still get a Touch ID sensor
which is really convenient for logging in

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:15.860
and not having to enter your password every
time macOS asks you for it.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:20.970
While the trackpad is a bit smaller than the
one on the Pro, it’s still the same industry-leading

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:25.580
ForceTouch trackpad that’s perhaps one of
the biggest advantages over Windows laptops.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:28.350
It’s seriously the best trackpad you can
get.

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:32.480
On top of that, if you value battery life,
the MacBook Air gets the best battery life

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:34.220
out of any MacBook.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:39.010
PCMag showed that it ran for 20 hours in their
battery life test, about an hour and a half

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:43.570
longer than the Pro, and completely wiping
the floor with other popular Windows laptops.

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:47.480
We tested the speakers various times and we
found that they’re actually pretty great,

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:56.620
especially compared to most Windows laptops.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:05:07.540
They’re not as bassy as the MacBook Pro’s
speakers, but they are more than good enough

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.990
to binge watch your favorite show on netflix.

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:15.410
So with the MacBook Air, you get a very comfortable
typing experience, standard function keys,

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:21.350
really good speakers, top-of-the-line battery
life, a decent display, the excellent trackpad

00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:27.690
and reliable macOS software, all for $1100
or $1000 with a student discount.

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:33.510
So how the heck was Apple able to drop the
price by $100 for a great laptop like this?

00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:35.480
Well here’s where the bad news comes in.

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:39.760
While testing storage speeds of this new MacBook
Air, we saw that they’ve become quite a

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:43.060
bit slower compared to SSDs from 2018 and
even 2017.

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:49.069
Even the 512GB model was limited to around
1300 MBps read and write.

00:05:49.069 --> 00:05:50.290
Now is this a big deal?

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:52.330
Actually, I don’t think so.

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:56.550
Yes, it does suck that storage speeds are
slower, but they’re still just as fast or

00:05:56.550 --> 00:05:58.860
faster than most Windows laptops.

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:04.510
And for the people this laptop is meant for,
like students, writers, programmers and common

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:07.540
people, the speeds are actually more than
fast enough.

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:12.710
You really only need faster storage speeds
for working with productivity apps like photoshop,

00:06:12.710 --> 00:06:16.830
Lightroom and Final Cut Pro, and if you’re
doing that, you should be buying a MacBook

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:17.830
Pro anyway.

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:21.430
So no, I don’t think the slower storage
speeds are a big deal at all.

00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:25.400
Overall, this is great laptop and probably
the best choice if you don’t need the extra

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:28.500
performance and would like to save a couple
hundred bucks.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:33.060
However, there is a third-wheel that just
entered the market, and that’s the 2018

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:38.261
iPad Pro loaded with Apple’s upcoming iPadOS
software, and I think it could actually make

00:06:38.261 --> 00:06:40.760
sense for some people to choose that instead.

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:44.620
If you haven’t seen that video, definitely
check it out right there.

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:48.740
If you enjoyed this review, tap the like button
and click the circle above to subscribe.

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:53.760
Thanks for watching and we’ll see you in
the next one!

